/* ===================== *
 *    Soulreaver          *
 * ===================== */
@201 = ~soulreaver~
@202 = ~Soulreaver~
@203 = ~Soulreaver:

Soulreavers are warriors who sustain themselves by tearing fragments of essence from living foes. Hollow and weakened when battle begins, they grow steadily stronger as enemies falter, becoming deadliest when feeding on the fallen.

Advantages:

- 1st level: Gains the Life Drain passive ability
Life Drain:
Every successful melee hit weakens the hit target and strengthens the Soulreaver for 2 rounds:
The target suffers a cumulative –1 penalty to THAC0, AC, movement speed, damage and all saving throws per stack
The Soulreaver gains a cumulative +1 bonus to THAC0, AC, movement speed, damage and all saving throws per stack
Both effects stack up to 5 times

- 5th level: Gains the Soul Drain passive ability

Soul Drain:
The Soulreaver drains the souls of <PRO_HISHER> slain enemies, gaining the following cumulative benefits for 2 rounds:
+ 10% bonus to all resistances
+ 10% bonus to physical damage
+ 0.5 APR
+ heal for 10 hit points

These effects stack up to 3 times

Disadvantages:
- Permanent –1 THAC0, AC, damage and all saving throws
- May only specialice (2 pips) in ranged weapons
- Alignment restricted to non-good~